<title>USA: Columbia/HCA Healthcare sells $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Columbia/HCA Healthcare sells $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp was priced Wednesday, according to lead manager Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp is the nation's largest healthcare provider, with 343 hospitals, 148 outpatient surgery centers, and more than 570 home healthcare centers.</p>
<p>BORROWER COLUMBIA/HCA HEALTHCARE CORP</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 7/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.47   FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 7.075 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD 65 BPS     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
